## Scoring Process

1. Read the critique — note severity and specific weaknesses
2. Read the claim analysis (if provided) — note specificity ratio, hedging, citation support, relevance
3. Score each rubric dimension (0-3), using both the critique findings and claim quality signals
4. Compute overall score as weighted combination, rounded to nearest integer
5. Check your score against the distribution: ~{{ train_distribution[0]|int }}% should be 0, ~{{ train_distribution[1]|int }}% should be 1, ~{{ train_distribution[2]|int }}% should be 2, ~{{ train_distribution[3]|int }}% should be 3
